<article class="article">
<p class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</p>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: Couples in Rainy Weather</h1>
<p>Rain is the part of Hanoi’s character that guidebooks photograph around, and a couple on a rented 50cc meets it sooner or later. The warm season’s script is familiar: a bright afternoon builds a grey-green sky, the vendors slide tarps over their crates, and twenty minutes later the streets are running and steaming at the same time. The verified 50cc rate is 200,000 VND per day, the counter at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien is open 09:00 to 21:00 daily, and a small shared bike in the rain is entirely manageable when the pair rides as a team rather than as a rider plus luggage.</p>
<p>This guide follows the couples series on the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental hub for Hanoi</a>, after <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/couples-choosing-a-50cc/">choosing a 50cc as a couple</a>, and it borrows the wider wet-weather playbook from the guide to <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/first-time-visitors-rainy-weather/">rainy-weather riding for first-time visitors</a>. For verified prices, the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost overview</a> has the numbers, and the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a> answers the general rental questions. Rain changes a shared ride in specific, learnable ways, and both seats have jobs in it.</p>
